WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:05.940
Sirens blared, and the loud ringing of the&nbsp;
emergency alarm system gave everyone a scare,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.940 --> 00:00:10.560
like something had jumped out at them&nbsp;
unexpectedly. With that fright came a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.560 --> 00:00:14.760
sharp jolt of adrenaline; something wasn’t&nbsp;
right, and their options were to either await&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.760 --> 00:00:20.400
instructions or try and flee with their lives.&nbsp;
Most took the latter, dropping their shovels and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:25.920
various mining tools so that they could turn heel&nbsp;
and bolt to the nearest opening. Outside, if they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.920 --> 00:00:31.500
could just get outside, above ground where the&nbsp;
air was a little clearer, then they could avoid…&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.500 --> 00:00:39.120
whatever it was that was happening. But, for Yuri,&nbsp;
escape wasn’t an option; he had to do something.&nbsp;

00:00:39.120 --> 00:00:44.700
It had been a standard operation, everything&nbsp;
had been run by the books and was going all the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.700 --> 00:00:49.680
smoother for it. But that noble approach hadn’t&nbsp;
stopped the drill from breaching into a cavern,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.680 --> 00:00:54.900
carving through stone into a previously&nbsp;
undiscovered cavern. That on its own&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.900 --> 00:01:00.240
wasn’t enough to cause concern; it was the&nbsp;
sudden cave-in that had triggered the alarms,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.240 --> 00:01:04.200
and led to the ensuing panic.
At the controls of the gigantic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.200 --> 00:01:09.540
excavation machine, Yuri helplessly pulled at&nbsp;
levers and pressed buttons, desperately trying to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.540 --> 00:01:16.080
undo the rapidly worsening damage. But it was too&nbsp;
late, rocks and debris were showering from above,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.080 --> 00:01:21.420
like the Earth itself was retaliating against the&nbsp;
mining workers. It was as if they shouldn’t have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.420 --> 00:01:26.940
drilled that deep, the cave-in almost like they&nbsp;
had awakened something… unfortunately for Yuri,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.940 --> 00:01:31.500
a falling slab of stone made sure&nbsp;
he wouldn’t get to see exactly what.&nbsp;

00:01:31.500 --> 00:01:35.280
The dust settled shortly after,&nbsp;
but only one recorded casualty,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.280 --> 00:01:40.380
along with multiple injured mine workers, wasn’t&nbsp;
enough to deter them from exploring what they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.380 --> 00:01:45.780
had accidentally stumbled upon. Venturing&nbsp;
into the cavern system pierced by the drill,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:45.780 --> 00:01:51.300
those who first dared to set foot down there&nbsp;
were greeted with the sight of strange,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.300 --> 00:01:57.660
crudely built stone structures. Someone had&nbsp;
been here before, but how? Nothing could&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.660 --> 00:02:04.620
survive this far below ground… nothing living,&nbsp;
nothing human at least. And that was true,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.620 --> 00:02:11.520
given that the workers also came across something&nbsp;
else in their initial exploration… human remains.&nbsp;

00:02:11.520 --> 00:02:16.920
Of course, this raised quite a concern, prompting&nbsp;
the workers to try and contact their superiors.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.920 --> 00:02:22.200
Uncovering bodies wasn’t exactly uncommon for&nbsp;
anyone whose job it was to dig into the ground,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.200 --> 00:02:27.480
so they at least had a protocol in place for&nbsp;
this kind of situation. What none of them were&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:27.480 --> 00:02:32.760
prepared for, however, was the fiery abomination&nbsp;
that suddenly emerged as they were trying to call&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.760 --> 00:02:38.760
for help. The creature was a nightmarish blend&nbsp;
of a humanoid shape, with the head of a dog and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.760 --> 00:02:44.280
giant wings much like a bat’s. Covered in&nbsp;
rough fur, its body was exuding an oily,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:44.280 --> 00:02:49.680
flammable substance… which it used to incinerate&nbsp;
the surviving mine workers in an instant.&nbsp;

00:02:49.680 --> 00:02:54.960
By the time that operatives of the SCP Foundation&nbsp;
arrived on the scene in the town of Mirny,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.960 --> 00:03:00.000
within the Sakha Republic, the creature was&nbsp;
on a rampage. Buildings were collapsing as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:05.700
the winged beast set the nearby area ablaze.&nbsp;
Troops on the ground, even once they were able&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:05.700 --> 00:03:10.740
to get the monster in range, found that their&nbsp;
conventional weapons were useless. It cost the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:10.740 --> 00:03:16.920
lives of seventeen Mobile Task Force operatives –&nbsp;
all immolated down to a cinder – before a chopper&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:16.920 --> 00:03:21.060
was able to neutralize the creature.
With the threat destroyed, and the town&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:21.060 --> 00:03:27.000
administered with amnestics and fed a convincing&nbsp;
cover story, you’d think that was case closed on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:27.000 --> 00:03:32.220
a job well done. But the Foundation discovered,&nbsp;
within the nearby Mirny mine, something that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:32.220 --> 00:03:37.980
would completely change everything they thought&nbsp;
they knew. Deep underground was a sinkhole,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:37.980 --> 00:03:44.160
leading to a spatial anomaly below, consisting of&nbsp;
the system of caverns that the mine workers had&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:44.160 --> 00:03:49.500
inadvertently stumbled upon. That wasn’t all that&nbsp;
the Foundation was about to discover down there;&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:49.500 --> 00:03:56.580
and what they came across would soon become&nbsp;
one of their darkest secrets: SCP-3667&nbsp;

00:03:56.580 --> 00:04:01.500
It wasn’t long before the Foundation began&nbsp;
encountering other unusual creatures that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:01.500 --> 00:04:07.500
seemingly appeared in the vicinity of SCP-3667.&nbsp;
However, not all of them matched the description&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:07.500 --> 00:04:12.360
of the original, bat-winged, dog-headed,&nbsp;
pyromaniacal visitor. Officially dubbed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:12.360 --> 00:04:18.720
as instances of SCP-3667-1, these creatures&nbsp;
ranged from the aforementioned monstrosity&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:18.720 --> 00:04:24.720
to a whole host of other strange descriptions.
One was an abnormally thin humanoid creature,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:24.720 --> 00:04:29.520
with reddish-brown skin and a head that was&nbsp;
too big for its wiry body. It possessed an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:29.520 --> 00:04:34.680
ordinary human level of intelligence, and even&nbsp;
spoke modern Russian, matching the common local&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:34.680 --> 00:04:40.380
dialect. In conversation, this being tried&nbsp;
to offer wealth or power in exchange for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:40.380 --> 00:04:45.480
a person’s most valued possessions. However,&nbsp;
it seemed to possess no anomalous abilities,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:45.480 --> 00:04:51.240
and would attempt to renegotiate a new offer&nbsp;
immediately after a bargain was made. Then,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:51.240 --> 00:04:56.220
there were the ‘magistrates’; a group of&nbsp;
forty-eight humanoids with kyphotic curved&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:56.220 --> 00:05:02.640
spines. All of them wore furs, and a variety of&nbsp;
skulls from animals such as elks, deer, and moose.&nbsp;

00:05:02.640 --> 00:05:07.740
The Foundation were still none the wiser as to&nbsp;
the true origin of all these different subspecies&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:07.740 --> 00:05:12.600
of creatures. They were obviously emanating from&nbsp;
the sinkhole, and the Foundation had been making&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:12.600 --> 00:05:20.820
use of MTF Chi-5, codenamed ‘Solomon’s SEALs’ to&nbsp;
eliminate instances of SCP-3667-1 that appeared&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:20.820 --> 00:05:26.100
from below. Surface-to-air missile systems were&nbsp;
even installed nearby, should any more flying&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:26.100 --> 00:05:32.400
creatures appear. But further exploration into the&nbsp;
sinkhole, and the caverns below, would only yield&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:32.400 --> 00:05:40.500
further questions… and even more strange entities.
The four-person unit MTF Chi-5 Team One was sent&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:40.500 --> 00:05:46.440
in to conduct preliminary exploration into&nbsp;
SCP-3667, to try and assess more accurately&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:46.440 --> 00:05:51.240
the threat level posed by the sinkhole and&nbsp;
its bizarre residents. Finding themselves&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:51.240 --> 00:05:55.920
in a large cave, the team followed the&nbsp;
sounds of running water to a wide stream,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:55.920 --> 00:06:01.200
the water a yellowish-grey in coloration. They&nbsp;
also detected the sound of numerous voices,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:01.200 --> 00:06:06.000
all whispering in Russian, but found it too&nbsp;
difficult to distinguish what they were saying.&nbsp;

00:06:06.000 --> 00:06:11.460
There were remains too, of some kind of structure&nbsp;
that seemed to indicate the existence of sentient&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:11.460 --> 00:06:18.540
life within SCP-3667. There was a portion of&nbsp;
a wall, even a hallway, that led into a large,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:18.540 --> 00:06:24.180
windowless, circular room. The floor of this&nbsp;
chamber featured an elaborate mosaic, that seemed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:24.180 --> 00:06:30.540
to have sustained some damage. But it depicted&nbsp;
anomalous creatures, including some that looked&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:30.540 --> 00:06:35.760
like the first winged monster that had appeared.
After splitting up down various corridors, two&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:35.760 --> 00:06:41.940
members of Team One encountered a new entity from&nbsp;
within SCP-3667. This creature resembled a large&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:41.940 --> 00:06:48.120
feline, but had no eyes, and was about ten meters&nbsp;
in height. It referred to the MTF operatives as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:48.120 --> 00:06:53.340
‘sinners’ and foolish mortals who should have&nbsp;
stayed in their cages. Despite being eyeless,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:53.340 --> 00:06:58.080
the creature observed that the Team did not&nbsp;
possess what it called the ‘Mark of Ognyena’,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:58.080 --> 00:07:02.580
and remarked that they should not have been&nbsp;
there. Feeling threatened by the creature,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:02.580 --> 00:07:07.080
MTF Chi-5 Team One were able to blow it&nbsp;
up with a grenade, before being safely&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:07.080 --> 00:07:13.380
retrieved by their fellow Foundation personnel.
Exploration into SCP-3667 was then resumed by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:13.380 --> 00:07:19.380
MTF Chi-5 Teams Two and Three, who were alarmed to&nbsp;
hear what sounded like a human scream coming from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:19.380 --> 00:07:24.960
somewhere within the caves. While they first&nbsp;
assumed it was another SCP-3667-1 creature,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:24.960 --> 00:07:29.340
someone suggested the possibility that&nbsp;
a civilian could have stumbled onto the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:29.340 --> 00:07:34.560
site of the Mirny mine before the Foundation had&nbsp;
arrived and established a secure perimeter around&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:34.560 --> 00:07:40.560
the sinkhole. Hearing the scream a second time,&nbsp;
this time further away, the MTF agents decided to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:40.560 --> 00:07:45.480
investigate, just in case an innocent person had&nbsp;
been dragged underground by one of the creatures.&nbsp;

00:07:45.480 --> 00:07:51.180
Passing through a basin of the same strange fluid&nbsp;
that Team One had discovered, the MTF Teams could&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:51.180 --> 00:07:56.640
hear more unsettling sounds coming from deep&nbsp;
within the caverns. In particular, a repetitive&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:56.640 --> 00:08:02.580
scratching noise… Next, they discovered a large,&nbsp;
intricate wooden structure, a circle with one side&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:02.580 --> 00:08:08.100
that appeared to be winched open. Inside, they&nbsp;
could see rows of wooden spikes, covered in a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:08.100 --> 00:08:13.140
dark liquid that everyone assumed was blood.
Hearing whimpers from their supposed missing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:13.140 --> 00:08:18.240
civilian, the team’s commander decided to call a&nbsp;
retreat. It was then that the MTF realized there&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:18.240 --> 00:08:24.060
were over twenty more wooden structures nearby.&nbsp;
Each was of a different shape and size, but all&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:24.060 --> 00:08:29.400
of them were covered in rats that were staring at&nbsp;
the Foundation operatives. These various pieces of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:29.400 --> 00:08:35.340
wooden apparatus seemed to resemble… torture&nbsp;
devices. And some of them had bodies inside.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:35.340 --> 00:08:40.080
The MTF agents thought they had discovered the&nbsp;
grisly fate of their missing civilian. Little&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:40.080 --> 00:08:46.020
did they know that things were far worse than they&nbsp;
first seemed; the bodies in the torture devices…&nbsp;

00:08:46.020 --> 00:08:50.580
…were still alive.
The Foundation soon realized that there were&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:50.580 --> 00:08:57.180
upwards of twelve thousand people within SCP-3667,&nbsp;
and immediately began efforts to rescue as many as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:57.180 --> 00:09:01.500
they could. Luckily, they had established&nbsp;
a field base on site in the mine, close&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:01.500 --> 00:09:08.040
enough to the sinkhole that led into SCP-3667.&nbsp;
However, the unfortunate reality was that saving&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:08.040 --> 00:09:12.900
all of these trapped human beings was no small&nbsp;
undertaking, and space at their nearby base,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:12.900 --> 00:09:19.200
Site 574, was limited. Only one hundred and fifty&nbsp;
of the people were able to be recovered and were&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:19.200 --> 00:09:26.880
transported to Site 574. Those that were had been&nbsp;
found trying to escape from SCP-3667, or being&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:26.880 --> 00:09:32.520
eaten by the various nightmarish creatures below.
But what quickly became apparent was that these&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:32.520 --> 00:09:39.480
people, those safely recovered from SCp-3667&nbsp;
and those still trapped within, weren’t exactly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:39.480 --> 00:09:46.680
ordinary. When Team One had discovered the strange&nbsp;
yellow-grey stream in SCP-3667, they had collected&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:46.680 --> 00:09:52.320
a sample of the fluid for analysis. Examining this&nbsp;
sample revealed an anomalous molecular structure,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:52.320 --> 00:09:58.020
that would actively bond with organic matter. And&nbsp;
this same unidentified molecule was present in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:58.020 --> 00:10:02.340
the bloodstream of the human beings found&nbsp;
beneath the sinkhole. It seemed to have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:02.340 --> 00:10:07.200
bestowed each one of them with an anomalous&nbsp;
ability for a limited form of regeneration.&nbsp;

00:10:07.200 --> 00:10:12.900
Their bodies could withstand far more damage than&nbsp;
an average, non-anomalous human. The Foundation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:12.900 --> 00:10:17.940
even experimented with introducing the anomalous&nbsp;
molecule into the blood of other test subjects,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:17.940 --> 00:10:23.160
but it didn’t have the same regenerative effect.&nbsp;
It was assumed that the regeneration was linked&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:23.160 --> 00:10:29.460
directly to some other factor, and the molecule&nbsp;
from the fluid only acted as a catalyst. As such,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:29.460 --> 00:10:36.360
every person recovered from the caverns was&nbsp;
given the collective designation of SCP-3667-2.&nbsp;

00:10:36.360 --> 00:10:41.880
Now, various subspecies of strange creatures and&nbsp;
a group of people whose bodies could regenerate,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:41.880 --> 00:10:47.280
both living in a system of caverns beneath&nbsp;
Mirny, Sakha Republic. Not to mention all the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:47.280 --> 00:10:53.940
wooden torture devices that were being used on&nbsp;
the SCP-3667-2s. Just what the hell was going on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:53.940 --> 00:10:59.400
here? And what was it that made this discovery&nbsp;
one of the Foundation’s darkest secrets? Well,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:59.400 --> 00:11:03.780
the answers to that could be discovered in&nbsp;
what they learned next about the anomalous&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:03.780 --> 00:11:08.400
people they’d recovered from the sinkhole.
As the Foundation continued its examination,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:08.400 --> 00:11:16.920
their researchers at Site 574 happened upon a&nbsp;
startling realization. The SCP-3667-2 people were&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:16.920 --> 00:11:23.100
perfect physical and genetic matches to former&nbsp;
residents of the nearby town of Mirny. In fact, of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:23.100 --> 00:11:28.380
the over twelve thousand total, only one thousand,&nbsp;
three hundred and twenty-eight didn’t appear to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:28.380 --> 00:11:34.500
correspond to any known person from the area. But&nbsp;
then, thousands of others all had proof of their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:34.500 --> 00:11:39.720
existence that the Foundation was able to recover&nbsp;
from the town’s public records. Dates of birth,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:39.720 --> 00:11:46.140
names, former places of residence, family,&nbsp;
and next of kin… along with dates of death.&nbsp;

00:11:46.140 --> 00:11:52.200
The SCP-3667-2 instances all claimed to&nbsp;
have spent their entire lives underground,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:52.200 --> 00:11:57.060
beneath the sinkhole where they were tortured&nbsp;
endlessly by nightmarish creatures. Their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:57.060 --> 00:12:01.380
bodies could regenerate the external damage&nbsp;
they received, meaning the torture would go&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:01.380 --> 00:12:07.080
on for days, months, or even years at a time.
When sampling bodies buried in local cemeteries,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:07.080 --> 00:12:12.300
the Foundation discovered that these were,&nbsp;
in fact, copies of deceased residents. But&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:12.300 --> 00:12:17.160
not everyone who had lived and died in Mirny.&nbsp;
Only those whose families had lived there for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:17.160 --> 00:12:23.340
at least two generations, and who – while they&nbsp;
were alive – were suspected of committing a crime,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:23.340 --> 00:12:28.800
but never convicted. There was one other&nbsp;
unifying factor too: during their lives,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:28.800 --> 00:12:34.260
these residents all had some affiliation with a&nbsp;
particular religious group known as the Light of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:34.260 --> 00:12:41.460
Five Heavens Russian Orthodox Church.
To put it simply: SCP-3667 was Hell.&nbsp;

00:12:41.460 --> 00:12:47.760
Following a number of other incursions&nbsp;
involving SCP-3667-1 creatures, the Foundation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:47.760 --> 00:12:52.620
was eventually able to open negotiations with&nbsp;
the entities in order to ensure the continued&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:52.620 --> 00:13:01.380
stability of SCP-3667. The former director of Site&nbsp;
574, Ndeye Bocoume, was appointed as the ‘Director&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:01.380 --> 00:13:06.840
of hell’ and placed in charge of overseeing&nbsp;
the anomaly. Under her watch, the Foundation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:06.840 --> 00:13:13.920
would supposedly be relocating the displaced&nbsp;
SCP-3667-2s to safe, classified locations&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:13.920 --> 00:13:19.620
where they could be reintegrated into society.
However, in an email from the Director of hell,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:19.620 --> 00:13:24.000
she proposed a solution to the Foundation’s&nbsp;
dwindling number of D Class Personnel.&nbsp;

00:13:24.000 --> 00:13:28.620
“I’m happy to announce that something&nbsp;
has come up that changes that – I’ll be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:28.620 --> 00:13:33.600
sending each of you a shipment of new D-Class&nbsp;
come next week. It isn’t as many as you had&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:33.600 --> 00:13:38.700
hoped for, but rest assured, these ones will&nbsp;
withstand most anything you throw at them…”&nbsp;

00:13:38.700 --> 00:13:45.180
Now go and check out “SCP-3000 - ANANTASHESHA”&nbsp;
and “SCP-096’S SAD END!” for more!

